WEBVTT

1
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.860
That's it? Three guys?

2
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.720
Two guys on the roof. Every guy gets a share, five shares is plenty.

3
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.160
Six shares. Don't forget the guy who planned the job.

4
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.480
He thinks he can sit it out and still take a slice.

5
00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.160
I know why they call him the Joker.

6
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.080
So why do they call him the Joker? I heard he wears makeup.

7
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.040
Makeup? Yeah, to scare people.

8
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:03.920
You know, war paint.

9
00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.560
Silent alarm.

10
00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.560
And there it goes.

11
00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.500
That's funny, it didn't dial out to 911.

12
00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.920
I was trying to reach a private number.

13
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.980
Is it a problem? No, I'm done here.

14
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:44.920
See,

15
00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.150
we don't want you doing anything with your hands other than...

16
00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.290
Right?

17
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.190
...thing up with like 5,000 volts.

18
00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:09.290
What kind of bank does that? A mob bank.

19
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.790
I guess the Joker's as crazy as they say.

20
00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.150
Where's the alarm guy? Boss told me when the guy was done, I should take him out.

21
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:16.870
One less share, right?

22
00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.270
Money. He told me something similar.

23
00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:21.770
No, no!

24
00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:38.320
That's a lot of money. If this Joker guy was so smart, he'd have had us bring a

25
00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:38.700
bigger cock.

26
00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.080
I'm betting the Joker told you to kill me as soon as we loaded the cash.

27
00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.340
No, no, no, no. I killed a bus driver.

28
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.380
Bus driver?

29
00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.040
What bus driver?

30
00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.280
School's out. Time to go.

31
00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.260
The guy's not getting up, is he?

32
00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.680
That's a lot of money.

33
00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.200
What happened to the rest of the guys?

34
00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.270
Think you're smart, huh?

35
00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.630
The guy that hired Hughes.

36
00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.050
He'll just do the same to you.

37
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.810
Oh, criminals in his town used to believe in things.

38
00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:29.730
Honor.

39
00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:31.310
Respect.

40
00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.770
Look at you. What are you believing, huh?

41
00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:41.070
What are you believing? I believe whatever doesn't kill you simply makes you a

42
00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:41.270
stranger.

43
00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.680
He did a campaign to clean up the city.

44
00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.220
When are you gonna start? Well, my guy, I believe, I already have.

45
00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.360
Like the so-called Batman, we're hearing that he's doing some good.

46
00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.300
Criminals are running scared, but I say no.

47
00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.200
No, man. I don't like it tonight.

48
00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.900
What, are you superstitious? You got more chance of winning the Powerball than

49
00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.960
running into him. That's simply just not true.

50
00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.040
I'm told that our men in the Major Crimes Unit are close to...

51
00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.940
It works. Mayor says you're closing in on the Batman.

52
00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:52.040
The investigation is ongoing.

53
00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:58.120
We're

54
00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.230
intending to see your wife again, Lieutenant.

55
00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.610
I thought you had to go look after your mother, Detective.

56
00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:07.690
Checked you back into the hospital.

57
00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:09.490
I'm sorry.

58
00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:13.470
So he hasn't shown up? He often doesn't.

59
00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.750
I like reminding everybody that he's out there.

60
00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:17.850
Why wouldn't you come?

61
00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.370
Hopefully. Because he's busy.

62
00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.050
That's why we bring dogs.

63
00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.090
I need them for a seat.

64
00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.950
Please, I beg you.

65
00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.870
Get them off! How would you do that?

66
00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:49.890
Stay with my customers.

67
00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:55.430
Buyer, beware. I told you my compound would take you places.

68
00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.910
I never said they'd be places you wanted to go.

69
00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.290
My business, to repeat, customers.

70
00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.310
You don't like what I have to offer.

71
00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.790
You can buy from someone else.

72
00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:08.070
Assuming Batman left anyone to buy from.

73
00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:10.250
My

74
00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.450
dogs are hungry!

75
00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.920
Maybe there's only one of them.

76
00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:31.370
That's not him.

77
00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.210
That's more like it.

78
00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.650
gives you the right? What's the difference between you and me?

79
00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:31.790
I'm not wearing hockey pants.

80
00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:42.500
Can't resist showing us his face.

81
00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.310
What's he hiding under that makeup?

82
00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.320
Can we get a minute, please?

83
00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:06.900
Another bunch of small timers.

84
00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.000
Some of the mark bills I gave you.

85
00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.280
My detectives have been making drug buys with them for weeks.

86
00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.400
This bank was another drop for the mob.

87
00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.880
That makes five. We found the bulk of their dirty cash.

88
00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:19.860
Time to move in. I'd have to head all banks simultaneously.

89
00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.080
SWAT teams, backup.

90
00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.160
What about this joker guy?

91
00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.160
One man or

92
00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:29.770
th- When the new D.A. hears about this, they'll want in.

93
00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:32.310
Do you trust him? It'll be hard to keep him out.

94
00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.310
And here he is, as stubborn as you are.

95
00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.660
Be nice when Wayne Manor's rebuilt.

96
00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:26.860
You can swap not sleeping in a penthouse to not sleeping in a mansion.

97
00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:31.180
Whenever you stitch yourself up, you do make a bloody mess.

98
00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.960
Yeah. It makes me learn from my mistakes.

99
00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:36.680
Well, you ought to be pretty knowledgeable by now, then.

100
00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:43.840
My armor, carrying too much weight, needs to be faster.

101
00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.180
I'm sure Mr. Fox can oblige.

102
00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:48.940
Did you get mauled by a tiger?

103
00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.360
It was a dog. Huh?

104
00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.760
It was a big dog.

105
00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:56.290
More copycats last night, Alfred, with guns.

106
00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.670
Why don't you hide them and take the weekend off?

107
00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:04.170
That wasn't exactly what I had in mind when I said I wanted to inspire people.

108
00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:04.910
I know.

109
00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.150
But things have been through. Look at the new district attorney.

110
00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:12.340
Closely.

111
00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:14.160
Need to know if he can be trusted.

112
00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.300
Are you interested in his character or his, uh, social circle?

113
00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.120
Who Rachel spends her time with is her business.

114
00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:29.340
I trust you don't have me followed on my day off.

115
00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.520
You ever took one, I might.

116
00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.240
Know your limits, Master Wayne.

117
00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.280
That man has no limits.

118
00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.620
Well, you do, sir. Well, can't afford to know him.

119
00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.140
Then what's gonna happen on the day that you find out?

120
00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.940
We all know how much you like to say, I told you so.

121
00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:50.140
On that day, Master Wayne, even I won't want to.

122
00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:51.420
Probably.

123
00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.500
Sorry I'm late, folks.

124
00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:07.060
Why were you? I'm worried he'd have to step up.

125
00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:09.180
Harvey, I know these briefs backwards.

126
00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.280
Well, fair's fair.

127
00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.660
Heads I'll take it, tails he's all yours.

128
00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.020
Oh, yeah? You wanna flip a coin to see who leads?

129
00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:20.740
It's my father's lucky coin. As I recall, I got me my first date with you.

130
00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.300
You wouldn't leave something like that up to Ch

131
00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:24.710
- I don't.

132
00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.090
I make my own luck.

133
00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:31.770
All rise. The Honorable Ned Creel providing.

134
00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.710
I thought the DA just played golf with a man, things like that.

135
00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:38.990
TF's 130. More than enough time to put you away for life, Sally.

136
00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.850
With Carmine, Falcone, and Arkham, someone must have stepped up to run the so-called

137
00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:43.250
family?

138
00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:46.690
Is that man in this courtroom today?

139
00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.560
Could you identify him for us, please?

140
00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.360
You win, Counselor.

141
00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:55.540
It was me.

142
00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:04.210
I have a sworn statement from you that this man, Salvatore Moroni, is

143
00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.010
the new head of the Falcone crime family.

144
00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:08.250
Moroni? He's a fall guy.

145
00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.050
I'm the brains of the organization.

146
00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:11.850
Order.

147
00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:13.950
Permission to treat the witness as hostile?

148
00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.770
Hostile? I'll show you hostile!

149
00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.620
Carbon fiber, 28 caliber, main china.

150
00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.160
If you want to kill a public servant, Mr.

151
00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.660
Moroni, I recommend you buy American.

152
00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:32.060
Get him out of here. But, Your Honor, I'm not done.

153
00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.380
We'll never build the lengthy gun to Moroni so we won't be able to charge him, but

154
00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:41.980
the fact that they're trying to kill you means we're getting to them.

155
00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.580
I'm not just so pleased, Rachel.

156
00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.440
I'm fine, by the way. Come on, Harvey.

157
00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:48.640
You're Gotham's D.A. You're not getting shot at.

158
00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:49.800
You're not doing your job right.

159
00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:54.850
You said you were rattled. We could take the rest of the way off.

160
00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:58.510
You can't. I dragged the head of the Major Crimes Unit down here.

161
00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:00.970
Oh, Jim Gordon? He's a friend, actually.

162
00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.330
Try to be nice.

163
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.150
I hear you got a hell of a right cross.

164
00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:20.170
It's a shame Sal's going to walk.

165
00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:23.610
Yeah, well, good thing about the mob is they keep giving you second chances.

166
00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.270
Lightly irradiated bills.

167
00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:34.230
Fancy stuff for a city cop.

168
00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.410
Have help? We liaise with various agencies.

169
00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.170
Save it, Gordon. I want to meet him.

170
00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:42.690
Official policy is to arrest the vigilante known as Batman on sight.

171
00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.430
And what about that floodlight on the top of MCU?

172
00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.870
Have you got problems with malfunctioning equipment?

173
00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:50.370
I suggest you take them up with maintenance, Counselor.

174
00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.770
I've put every known money launderer in Gotham behind bars, but the mob is still

175
00:16:54.770 --> 00:17:00.690
getting its money out. I think you and your friend have found the last game in town

176
00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:01.930
and you're trying to hit them where it hurts.

177
00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:03.710
They're wallets. It's bold.

178
00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.900
You gonna count me in? In this town, the fewer people know something, the safer the

179
00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:13.020
operation. Gordon, I don't like that you've got your own special unit.

180
00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.020
And I don't like that it's full of cops I investigated at Internal Affairs.

181
00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:19.160
If I didn't work with cops you'd investigate it while you were making your name at I

182
00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.200
.A. I'd be working alone.

183
00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:23.360
I don't get political points for being an idealist.

184
00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.180
I have to do the best I can with what I have.

185
00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:33.940
You want me to back warrants for search and seizure on five banks without telling me

186
00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:34.500
what we're after?

187
00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:38.120
I can give you the names of the banks.

188
00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:39.720
Well, that's a start.

189
00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.180
I'll get you your warrants, but I want your trust.

190
00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:44.960
You don't have to sell me debt.

191
00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:47.220
We all know you're Gotham's white knight.

192
00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.790
I heard they have a different name for me down at MCU.

193
00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:53.610
I would love that.

194
00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:59.010
In China, Lao Security Investment stands for Dynamic New Growth.

195
00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:02.410
A joint Chinese venture with Wien Enterprises will be a powerhouse.

196
00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:04.450
Well, Mr. Lao,

197
00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:09.870
I speak for the rest of the board and Mr.

198
00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.750
Wien in expressing our own excitement.

199
00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.150
I know that Mr. Wien is curious about how his trust fund gets replenished, but

200
00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.230
frankly, this is embarrassing.

201
00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:25.230
You worry about the diligence, Mr.

202
00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:27.650
Rees. I'll worry about Bruce Wayne.

203
00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:29.330
It's done.

204
00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:31.810
The numbers are solid.

205
00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:33.270
Do them again.

206
00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:35.610
Wouldn't want the trust fund to run out.

207
00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:36.010
Another

208
00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.840
long night?

209
00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.460
This joint venture was your idea.

210
00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.400
The consultants love it. But I'm not convinced.

211
00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.140
Lao's company has grown by 8% annually like clockwork.

212
00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.480
His revenue stream must be off the books.

213
00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.280
Maybe even illegal.

214
00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.180
Okay, cancel the deal.

215
00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.660
You already knew.

216
00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.280
I just needed a closer look at their books.

217
00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:03.980
Anything else you can trouble me for?

218
00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:05.760
I need a new suit.

219
00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:08.880
Three buttons is a little 90s, Mr.

220
00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:10.940
Wayne. I'm not talking in fashion, Mr.

221
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.140
Fox. So much is function.

222
00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.960
You want to be able to turn your head.

223
00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.080
Short me backing out of the driveway easier.

224
00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:18.760
I'll see what I can do.

225
00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:26.070
Took me three weeks to get a reservation here.

226
00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:27.930
And I had to tell him I worked for the government.

227
00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:30.970
Really? The city health inspector's not afraid to pull strings.

228
00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.390
Rachel. Fancy that.

229
00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:34.570
Yeah, Bruce.

230
00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:38.570
Fancy that. Rachel, Natasha, Natasha, Rachel.

231
00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:39.310
Natasha,

232
00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:41.730
are you the prima...

233
00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:43.510
Prima ballerina for the Moscow ballet.

234
00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:45.770
Wow. Harvey's taking me next week.

235
00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:47.830
Really? So you're in a ballet.

236
00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.210
Bruce, this is Harvey Dent.

237
00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:52.110
The famous Bruce Wayne.

238
00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.470
Rachel's told me everything about you.

239
00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.810
I certainly hope not. So let's put a couple tables together.

240
00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.470
I'm not sure that they'll let us.

241
00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.550
Oh, they should. I own the place.

242
00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.970
How could you want to raise children in a city...

243
00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.260
this? Well, I was raised here.

244
00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:09.820
I turned out okay. Is Wayne Manor in the city limits?

245
00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.480
The Palisades? Sure.

246
00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:17.340
You know, as our new DA, you might want to figure out where your jurisdiction ends.

247
00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:21.900
I'm talking about the kind of city that idolizes a masked vigilante.

248
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:25.380
Gotham City is proud of an ordinary citizen standing up for what's right.

249
00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:29.540
Gotham needs heroes like you, elected officials, not a man who thinks he is above

250
00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.300
the law. Exactly. Who appointed the Batman?

251
00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:35.560
We did. All of us who stood by and let scum take control of our city.

252
00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:37.520
But this is a democracy, Harvey.

253
00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:41.400
When their enemies were at the gates, the Romans would suspend democracy and appoint

254
00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:42.600
one man to protect the city.

255
